---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";

const contactEmail = "tymurbogach@gmail.com";
const updatedAt = "November 4, 2026";
---

<Layout
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description="Privacy policy for Nastymur services operated by Tymur Bogach."
>
  <article class="mx-auto w-full max-w-4xl py-6 laptop:py-12 laptop-scaled:py-12">
    <header class="mb-10 border-b border-[var(--border)] pb-8">
      <p class="font-hud mb-3 text-xs font-bold tracking-[0.35em] text-[var(--foreground-faint)] uppercase">
        Nastymur
      </p>
      <h1 class="mb-4 text-4xl leading-tight font-bold text-[var(--foreground)] mobile:text-5xl">
        Privacy Policy
      </h1>
      <p class="m-0 text-sm text-[var(--foreground-faint)]">
        Last updated: {updatedAt}
      </p>
    </header>

    <div class="space-y-10 text-[0.95rem] leading-7 text-[var(--muted-foreground)] mobile:text-base">
      <section>
        <h2 class="mb-3 text-2xl font-semibold text-[var(--foreground)]">
          Who operates these services
        </h2>
        <p>
          Tymur Bogach operates Nastymur services: this portfolio site,
          JobPilot, and LazyTripZ. For privacy questions or data deletion
          requests, email
          <a
            class="font-medium text-[var(--accent)] underline underline-offset-4"
            href={`mailto:${contactEmail}`}
          >
            {contactEmail}
          </a>
          .
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="mb-3 text-2xl font-semibold text-[var(--foreground)]">
          This portfolio site
        </h2>
        <p>
          This site uses self-hosted Umami analytics to count page views and
          visitors. It does not use advertising cookies or cross-site tracking.
          Aggregated visit counts are shown on the home page.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-4">
          The color theme and light/dark mode choice are stored in your
          browser's local storage. They never leave your device.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-4">
          Messages sent through the contact form include your name, email
          address, and message. They are delivered through Web3Forms so your
          message reaches the site operator. Do not include sensitive personal
          data in the form.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-4">
          Messages sent to the on-site chat are processed in memory to generate
          a reply and are not stored permanently. Chat history expires
          automatically after a short period.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="mb-3 text-2xl font-semibold text-[var(--foreground)]">
          How Nastymur handles Google user data
        </h2>
        <p>
          Nastymur apps use Google Sign-In to authenticate you. They receive
          your Google account identifier, name, email address, and profile
          picture, and use this data to create and secure your account. OAuth
          tokens are encrypted before storage. The services run on private,
          self-hosted infrastructure and do not sell your data, use it for
          advertising, or share it with unrelated third parties.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-4">
          The use and transfer of information received from Google APIs follows
          the
          <a
            class="font-medium text-[var(--accent)] underline underline-offset-4"
            href="https://developers.google.com/terms/api-services-user-data-policy"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener noreferrer"
          >
            Google API Services User Data Policy
          </a>
          , including its Limited Use requirements.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="mb-3 text-2xl font-semibold text-[var(--foreground)]">
          JobPilot
        </h2>
        <p>
          JobPilot can optionally connect your Gmail account with read-only
          access to find job-related messages. It reads message metadata such
          as sender, subject, date, and identifiers. JobPilot never sends,
          edits, or deletes your emails. Disconnecting Gmail stops future
          access; previously imported metadata remains until you delete it or
          your account.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-4">
          <a
            class="font-medium text-[var(--accent)] underline underline-offset-4"
            href="https://jobpilot.nastymur.com/privacy"
          >
            Full JobPilot privacy policy
          </a>
          {" · "}
          <a
            class="font-medium text-[var(--accent)] underline underline-offset-4"
            href="https://jobpilot.nastymur.com/terms"
          >
            JobPilot terms
          </a>
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="mb-3 text-2xl font-semibold text-[var(--foreground)]">
          LazyTripZ
        </h2>
        <p>
          LazyTripZ stores the trips you create: destinations and dates,
          activities, pets, diary entries, weather forecasts, and generated
          recommendations. Recommendations are generated with the Google Gemini
          API, which receives the destination, dates, and trip details. City
          names are sent to OpenWeatherMap and Nominatim/OpenStreetMap for
          weather and search.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-4">
          <a
            class="font-medium text-[var(--accent)] underline underline-offset-4"
            href="https://lazytripz.nastymur.com/privacy"
          >
            Full LazyTripZ privacy policy
          </a>
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="mb-3 text-2xl font-semibold text-[var(--foreground)]">
          Retention and deletion
        </h2>
        <p>
          Data is kept only while it supports an active account or the stated
          purpose. You can request deletion of your account and stored service
          data by emailing
          <a
            class="font-medium text-[var(--accent)] underline underline-offset-4"
            href={`mailto:${contactEmail}`}
          >
            {contactEmail}
          </a>
          .
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="mb-3 text-2xl font-semibold text-[var(--foreground)]">
          Policy changes
        </h2>
        <p>
          This page will show material changes to this policy. The date at the
          top shows the latest revision.
        </p>
      </section>
    </div>
  </article>
</Layout>
